step setup wezterm --theme ken --config-dir {SANDBOX}/config/wezterm
exit 1
stdout
stderr
| error: WezTerm already uses a theme sf2-themes does not manage, and sf2-themes will not edit it for you.
| Add this integration to {SANDBOX}/config/wezterm/wezterm.lua at the top level, after config is created and before the file returns it:
| 
| local sf2_current = "{SANDBOX}/config/wezterm/sf2-theme/wezterm-current-<digest>.lua"
| wezterm.add_to_config_reload_watch_list(sf2_current)
| local sf2_scheme = dofile(sf2_current)
| config.color_scheme = sf2_scheme
| local sf2_env = config.set_environment_variables or {}
| sf2_env.TERM_THEME = (type(sf2_scheme) == "string" and sf2_scheme:find("-light", 1, true)) and "light" or "dark"
| config.set_environment_variables = sf2_env
| 
| Remove the other color_scheme assignments, so this one selects the theme.
| 
| Then run the command again.
